---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy & notices"
  description="Privacy, simulation limits and rights information for the ContinuumOS website."
>
  <section class="page-intro wrap">
    <span class="section-label">WEBSITE NOTICE / {site.reviewed}</span>
    <h1>
      Local concepts.
      <br />
      <span class="mint">Clear boundaries.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This notice covers this static website and its browser playground. It is not a privacy or
      security promise for a finished operating system.
    </p>
  </section>
  <div class="page-content wrap">
    <section class="article-block">
      <h2>What the playground does</h2>
      <p>
        Editor text, mock files, appearance choices and simulated update history live in browser
        memory for the current page. Refreshing or leaving the page discards them. This site does
        not save them to local storage, cookies or a server.
      </p>
      <p>
        The playground does not access your filesystem, execute entered code or connect to a running
        OS. All desktop scenes, generations and update events are illustrations. They are not guest
        screenshots, uptime evidence or performance results.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="article-block">
      <h2>Hosting and external links</h2>
      <p>
        We add no analytics, advertising, tracking pixels, accounts or mailing-list forms. GitHub
        Pages hosts the site and processes visitor connection data under{' '}
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">
          GitHub’s privacy statement
        </a>
        . GitHub documents that Pages visitors’ IP addresses are logged for security purposes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Following a link to GitHub or another external site is subject to that service’s own
        policies. Project fonts and artwork are served with the website rather than requested from a
        font or image-tracking service.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="article-block">
      <h2>Identity and rights</h2>
      <p>
        ContinuumOS is a working project name. Continuum-Foundry is a GitHub namespace; this site
        does not claim incorporation, registered trademarks or a completed product release.
      </p>
      <p>
        Original material is all rights reserved. Third-party packages retain their own terms,
        recorded in the <a href={site.repository}>website repository</a>. External patches are
        currently paused. Public visibility does not grant a general source, artwork or trademark
        license.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
